    "description": "J-Express is a free, browser-based platform for interactive exploration, visualization and analysis of high-dimensional biological data, including bulk and single-cell RNA sequencing datasets. It provides principal component analysis (PCA), correspondence analysis, UMAP, hierarchical clustering, k-means, self-organizing maps, differential expression analysis, gene set enrichment analysis and interactive heatmaps.\n\nJ-Express combines classical statistical methods with modern machine learning, including text embeddings and semantic search. Through its Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration, AI assistants can interact with datasets, perform analyses and interpret results.\n\nDeveloped by Resonalis, J-Express runs directly in the web browser without requiring installation or programming skills. Data processing is performed locally in the browser, enabling interactive analysis without uploading datasets to a remote server.",
